7592186078673 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078673 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Linear Equations by Clearing a Rational Expression" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078673 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186079531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078673 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078673 #edb/ref 1050 780.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078673 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "2828ce66-5563-59d5-8c3e-194de1b4bc11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078918 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186076286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078918 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44320" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078918 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078918 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $\\frac{8y+5}{3}=6y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078918 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "15d287cc-b41b-5ff3-a7dc-97c2e50422d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078918 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8y+5}{3} & =6y \\\\ 3(\\frac{8y+5}{3}) & =3\\cdot 6y \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{8y+5}{\\cancel{3}}) & =18y \\\\ 8y+5 & =18y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8y+5 & =18y \\\\ 8y+5-8y & =18y-8y \\\\ 5 & =10y \\\\ \\frac{5}{10} & =\\frac{10y}{10} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079531 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079531 #edb/ref 1061 52855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079531 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "354b4bf1-8360-5dc0-abda-b916470adda6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079531 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186079717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079532 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079532 #edb/ref 1061 52856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079532 #edb/r