 [17592186496099 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186495865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496099 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3de57bae-a1f3-5ae4-b2cb-ef29b2469101" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496203 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496203 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496203 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186495892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496203 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e82146a9-b8b1-5e83-aeec-05796f3d090e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496249 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496249 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171600" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496249 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496249 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\frac{3k-2}{6}=-(k+2),$ then $k=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496249 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "470fa283-2b00-51e0-9a35-7c42b40fff42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496249 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $6$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3k-2}{6} & =-(k+2) \\\\ 6\\cdot (\\frac{3k-2}{6}) & =6\\cdot (-(k+2)) \\\\ \\cancel{6}\\cdot (\\frac{3k-2}{\\cancel{6}}) & =-6(k+2) \\\\ 3k-2 & =-6k-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k-2 & =-6k-12 \\\\ 3k-2+6k & =-6k-12+6k \\\\ 9k-2 & =-12 \\\\ 9k-2+2 & =-12+2 \\\\ 9k & =-10 \\\\ \\frac{9k}{9} & =\\frac{-10}{9} \\\\ k & =-\\frac{10}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496271 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496271 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104472" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496271 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496271 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $h$ where $\\frac{3h-4}{2}=2-h.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496271 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6bdf897b-5216-5fe0-b918-3faeb980f813" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496271 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $2.$ We must make sure that all of the terms on the right-hand side are multiplied by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3h-4}{2} & =2-h \\\\ 2\\cdot (\\frac{3h-4}{2}) & =2\\cdot (2-h) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot (\\frac{3h-4}{\\cancel{2}}) & =2\\cdot 2-2\\cdot h \\\\ 3h-4 & =4-2h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3h-4 & =4-2h \\\\ 3h-4+2h & =4-2h+2h \\\\ 5h-4 & =4 \\\\ 5h-4+4 & =4+4 \\\\ 5h & =8 \\\\ \\frac{5h}{5} & =\\frac{8}{5} \\\\ h & =\\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496277 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496277 #edb/ref 1069 "q-31686" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496277 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496277 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{5-x}{3}=7x-15.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496277 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e49ab95-b651-5531-ac5c-90e4392b7705" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496277 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $7$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-x}{3} & =7x-15 \\\\ 3(\\frac{5-x}{3}) & =3(7x-15) \\\\ \\cancel{3}(\\frac{5-x}{\\cancel{3}}) & =21x-45 \\\\ 5-x & =21x-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-x & =21x-45 \\\\ 5-x+x & =21x-45+x \\\\ 5 & =22x-45 \\\\ 5+45 & =22x-45+45 \\\\ 50 & =22x \\\\ \\frac{50}{22} & =\\frac{22x}{22} \\\\ \\frac{25}{11} & =\\frac{\\cancel{22}x}{\\cancel{22}} \\\\ x & =\\frac{25}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496333 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496333 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44329" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496333 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496333 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $t$ where $-2t=\\frac{4-6t}{9}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496333 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fcf291ca-08c9-536b-b233-ba6182878dc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496333 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $9$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2t & =\\frac{4-6t}{9} \\\\ \\frac{4-6t}{9} & =-2t \\\\ 9(\\frac{4-6t}{9}) & =9(-2t) \\\\ \\cancel{9}(\\frac{4-6t}{\\cancel{9}}) & =-18t \\\\ 4-6t & =-18t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-6t & =-18t \\\\ 4-6t+6t & =-18t+6t \\\\ 4 & =-12t \\\\ -12t & =4 \\\\ \\frac{-12t}{-12} & =\\frac{4}{-12} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-12}t}{\\cancel{-12}} & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ t & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496350 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186496374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496350 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6028f492-ba55-501f-87da-d15709c17c82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496350 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496357 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186496387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496357 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7206ffec-4e93-51d5-9045-454b39491a19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496357 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186496271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496358 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186496350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496358 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "799a2f4f-2697-5ff1-b785-172536801285" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496358 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186496277 #ed